  evidence:
    title: Unlisted Operator / Evidence case
    question: Which explanation fits all three signed records?
    clueNodes:
    - n22
    - n9
    - n19
    clues:
    - Payroll lists technician 441 alive at 08:10.
    - Dispatch shows 441 rejecting a rehearsal order at 08:14.
    - The identity mirror deletes 441 at 08:15, signed by a supervisor.
    answers:
    - id: accident
      title: The records disagree because of an ordinary clerical error.
      feedback: A clerical error does not explain the matching signed authorizations and their order.
      correct: 0
    - id: insider
      title: A lone outsider forged every record after the event.
      feedback: The independent receipt and earlier signatures rule out a single later forgery.
      correct: 0
    - id: rehearsal
      title: The registry was deliberately changed after a refusal.
      feedback: The technician was real. Their identity was removed after they refused an emergency rehearsal.
      correct: 1
  revelation: The technician was real. Their identity was removed after they refused an emergency rehearsal.
